## Palm Springs Lemon Law and Used Vehicles

Most states only offer lemon law benefits to defective vehicles purchased new. California lemon law extends to used vehicles sold with a dealer warranty.

## Dealer Warranty

Most dealerships in California sell used vehicles with a warranty that is good for 30 days or before 1,000 miles accrue on the odometer, whichever comes first. If you buy a used vehicle that meets the qualifications of CA lemon law within these terms, you may have a valid claim.

## Used Car Lemon Law Rights

Should your vehicle meet the qualifications of CA lemon law within the terms of the dealer warranty, you may be entitled to a buyback and all attorney/court costs.

## “As Is” Agreements

If you purchased your used vehicle with an “as is” agreement - specified on the buyer’s guide - you may not have any coverage under Palm Springs lemon law.

